--SPOILERS FOLLOW--                                    


The blindfold was probably the single most crucial item!  The combination of
polymorph and polymorph control rings was fun for a while, but eventually I
got tired of having my stats re-arranged and my name changed. I also lost my
first set of GDSM by forgetting to take it off before turning into a Marilith
(but it was fun!). I was surprised to discover that genociding L's prevented
me from turning into one thereafter! I got invis and see invis by eating a
pair of stalkers.

I got Excalibur from a fountain (it was very useful to have a rustproof
weapon!), Stormy from a bones level and Mojo from a wish (I seem to recall I
got one early on from a djinn).  I was reasonably lucky in finding shops
(which I standardly rob using the holes-in-the-walls trick) and altars. I got
my AC up to -34 by repeated good works (I poly'd into a Leprechaun and got my
money back on one occasion, but when I tried this in another temple the
priestess got angry). 

The Castle level took a while to get through, but was certainly worth it for
the WOW.  First wish: blessed scrolls of charging (had one left at the end).
Second wish: wand of polymorph, which got me a GDSM (given the kind of
critters who hang our down there!).  Third wish: blessed scrolls of enchant
armour (particularly to apply to the Helm of Brilliance and Gauntlets of
Dexterity). Fourth wish: amultet of lifesaving (which I never needed).  Fifth
wish: blessed luckstone.  I think this was a very good move, becuase I was
much more sucessful at casting spells after that! Still had a wish left at
the end (I suppose I could have upped my score by wishing for a lot of gold
at the last moment!).

My only `abuse' was polypiling, which I tried out mainly because I never had
the chance before!  This was useful for getting a full set of armour and a
couple of handy rings, namely teleport control (which I *really* needed,
having foolishly eaten a tengu - not being able to 'port on the Castle level
was a godsend to me!) and conflict (which was handy but not vital). It also
meant that I'd identified practically every item in the game except a few of
the spellbooks!

Speaking of spells, the general feeling is that they're useless, and on the
whole I agree, but actually one or two were really handy, in particular remove
curse (for when the Wiz had cursed my blindfold!) and magic mapping (which
helped me getting up through the hell levels).  The power-point system is
pointless, however, since the only limiting factor is the spells wearing out.

I found the Wizard on level 50 :-{ which meant he chased me all the way back
up. I had to kill him half a dozen times, but it wasn't hard with speed boots
and Stormy.  I was sorry not to have time to do Vlad's Tower, but with the Wiz
on my tail it wasn't worth it.  (I considered wishing for a potion of
paralysis to get rid of him, but that seemed like cheating!). 

The Endlevel was a piece of cake; I magic mapped it to see where to go, the
poly'd myself into a Xorn and just walked through the walls!

On the whole, I think I was a bit over-cautious with this character, but at
least I've done it now.  Finally I can get on with some work :-)

